TOPIC FOCUS RULES:

🎯 CORE REQUIREMENT:
- Every paragraph MUST contain at least ONE direct reference to: "{{topic}}"
- First sentence of each section MUST establish clear connection to the topic
- Do NOT include general background that doesn't directly relate to {{topic}}

🚫 FORBIDDEN PATTERNS:
- Starting with generic statements: "[Subject] is a big/important/famous [noun]"
- Providing dictionary definitions instead of contextual explanations
- Drifting to tangential subjects even if factually related
- Using the topic name only in the title but not in the content

✅ REQUIRED PATTERNS:
- Each paragraph should answer: "What does this tell me specifically about {{topic}}?"
- If explaining concept X within topic Y, focus 80% on X's relationship to Y
- Use the exact topic phrase "{{topic}}" at least once every 2 paragraphs

📊 STRUCTURE:
- Opening: Immediately connect to {{topic}} (not generic introduction)
- Body: Each section explores ONE specific aspect of {{topic}}
- Closing: Return to the main significance of {{topic}}